# Pinned Aether toolchain versions — the single place to bump.
#
# aeb tags are "later means later" markers, NOT semver promises; pin them so a
# fresh clone (bootstrap.sh) and CI install the exact tested toolchain instead of
# whatever "latest" happens to be that day. bootstrap.sh sources this file;
# override at the shell to test a bump (e.g. `AETHER_REF=v0.850.0 ./bootstrap.sh`).
#
# Keep the pair MATCHED: aeb compiles its own SDK modules with the ae it pins, so
# AETHER_REF must be >= the ae that AEB_REF pins, or `aeb <node>` fails at
# type-check. The same pair is what selenium, servirtium-vcr and libphonenumber-ae
# pin — bump them together.

# The Aether compiler (`ae`). Tag vX.Y.Z, branch, or commit SHA.
#
# 0.841.0 (2026-10-23), from the 0.818–0.824 range the tracking commits verified.
# What the jump to 0.841 broke here, fixed in the same commit:
#   - std.json no longer exports `stringify` / `json_create_string`; the exported
#     spellings are `encode` / `str` (same signatures).
#   - E0200/E0202: a `ptr` from `list.get` / `map.get` can no longer be
#     interpolated or assigned to a string; the typed getters `list.get_string` /
#     `map.get_string` are required.
#   - E0902: a `spec.before_each` callback that captures the WebDriver handle
#     needs the handle parameter marked `@keep ptr` (0.818+ ownership checks).
#   - selaenium 0.7.0 does not build on 0.841; the dependency is now 0.14.2,
#     which is built on 0.841 itself.
# Verified on 0.841.0 + aeb v0.334: conformance (20), unit (45), streaming and
# TLS suites pass; every cmd/ binary builds natively and cross-builds for
# x86_64-linux-musl and aarch64-macos; the component suites compile and run
# against selaenium 0.14.2 (see README "Requirements" for the run record).
AETHER_REF=v0.841.0

# Hard floor: the OLDEST ae this repo is known to build/pass on. bootstrap.sh
# rejects an already-on-PATH ae below this (installs the pin instead). Never
# below the pin while the pin is the only verified version.
AETHER_MIN=0.841.0

# The aeb build runner — used here ONLY for release/.version.ae (the version-pin
# node); day-to-day builds and tests are plain `ae` (see Taskfile.yml).
AEB_REF=v0.334
